{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Accidental Humanitarians", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Live Your Values", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 10, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 7, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.2", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "  Describe necessity, duty, advice, or strong disapproval in written and spoken situations according to work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "progress report ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a written document that explains the state of a project", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: As requested, here is a short progress report from our home base here in Lesotho.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le07ob10aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use when writing a summary of a humanitarian trip.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "missive", "type": "name"}, {"content": "an official letter", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: In fact, I'm scribbling this missive on a piece of paper on a bus.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le07ob10aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "setback", "type": "name"}, {"content": "something that causes a delay", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We've had a few small setbacks.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le07ob10aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "groundbreaking ceremony", "type": "name"}, {"content": "an event to mark the official start of a building project", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The groundbreaking ceremony for the medical center was supposed to have occurred on Saturday.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le07ob10aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "goodwill", "type": "name"}, {"content": "friendly or positive feelings", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Hopefully we generated a little awareness and goodwill within the community.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le07ob10aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "heartwarming", "type": "name"}, {"content": "describing feelings of kindness or happiness", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: What a heartwarming experience! ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le07ob10aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to make due ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to get along with what is available", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The children don't have a lot of modern amenities, but they make due with their limited resources.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le07ob10aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"content": "engenn10le07ob10re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Causative Verbs: Get and Have", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " You use the causative verbs<span class=\"italic\"> get</span> and<span class=\"italic\"> have </span>when you talk about  arranging for someone to do something for you.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Look at the following examples:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">I cleaned my room</span>. (Meaning: I cleaned it myself).", "type": "text"}, {"content": "If you paid or asked someone to do something,  you can say: <br/> <span class=\"italic\">(A cleaner) cleaned my room.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can use another way ( a causative construction): <br/> <span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">had </span>my room cleaned.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can also use the structure </span class=\"italic\">subject + have + person + verb</span> to identify <span class=\"strong\"> who </span>did the action.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">had the plumber fix </span>my sink.</span> <br/> <span class=\"italic\">The director <span class=\"strong\">had the employees prepare </span>a book report.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use the structures <span class=\"strong\"><span class=\"italic\">get</span> </span>+ <span class=\"italic\">object </span>+ <span class=\"italic\">past participle </span>(get something done) or <span class=\"strong\"><span class=\"italic\">get </span></span>+<span class=\"italic\"> person </span>+<span class=\"italic\"> to </span>+ <span class=\"italic\">verb </span>(get someone to do something).", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The causative verbs <span class=\"italic\">get </span>and <span class=\"italic\">have</span> are the same. Sometimes, <span class=\"italic\">get </span>has the feeling that you needed to convince someone to do something, while <span class=\"italic\">have </span>is more neutral.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "He got the local chiefs and politicians to rearrange their schedules so that they could attend.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "He had the workers completely drain the site so that we could set up some chairs for the press.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Samuel and I had the driver take us to two different foster homes.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Absence of Necessity", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " You use <span class=\"italic\">don't have to </span>and <span class=\"italic\">don't need to </span>to talk about absence of necessity, when something is unnecessary.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Look at the examples:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">don't have to </span>go to work today. It is Sunday. </span> <br/> <span class=\"italic\">He <span class=\"strong\">didn't have to </span>work yesterday, so he came to the movies with us.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">don't need to </span>go to the store today. We have enough groceries.</span> <br/> <span class=\"italic\">We <span class=\"strong\">don't need to </span>wash the car - it's clean.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "In the examples above, <span class=\"italic\">need </span>is the main verb. Sometimes  <span class=\"italic\">need</span> in the negative is used as a <span class=\"italic\">modal verb </span>(needn't).", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">She <span class=\"strong\">needn't worry</span>. Everything is OK.</span><br/> <span class=\"italic\">You <span class=\"strong\">needn't shout</span>. I can hear you.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "We didn't have to postpone, but we thought it wise under the circumstances.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "We really needn't worry about the future of the projects with him around!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "It just goes to show you that we don't need to have all of our modern toys and technologies in order to find a bit of contentment.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I don't have to tell you that time flies around here.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Imagine that you are on a humanitarian mission in the country of your choice.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write a list of at least three projects that you would like to complete in your chosen country.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write a mock progress report outlining the status of each one of your projects.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I create three humanitarian projects.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write a progress report.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I add vocabulary common on a humanitarian trip.", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " I can talk about social issues and moral dilemmas. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about having or getting something done.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can express what is not necessary. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " Do you know anything about the country of Lesotho?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": " If you were taking a trip to Lesotho, what would you bring?", "type": "Free Header Item"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}, {"content": " Ask your partner:", "type": "free_header_text"}, {"content": " Amy checks in from Lesotho!", "type": "free_type_text_area"}], "img_path": "", "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "id": 0, "stimuli_ids": [0]}, {"template_override": 1, "type": "STI", "questions": [{"responses": [{"correct": 0, "_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0, "id": 0}, {"correct": 1, "_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0, "id": 1}], "_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}]}], "id": 0}], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " \nAmy writes a report <span class=\"tool-tip\" id=\"tip_1_0\">on the fly</span>.\n", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Content", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": 